      "id": "C14",
      "title_zh": "生成对选择的递归影响",
      "title_en": "Recursive influence of generation on selection",
      "claim_zh": "活动后果可改变后继形成与选择条件，贡献变体不必获益。重构、发育与聚合区分遗传群体和运输集合；细菌回复实验接通遗传切换与周期完成。谱系预测保留对阶段和区组模型的总体优势；跨日期发育估计暴露前阶段迁移失败，常规解释获完整信用。",
      "claim_en": "Consequences can change successor formation and selection without guaranteeing contributor advantage. Reconstruction, development and aggregation distinguish inherited clusters from transport groups; bacterial reversion links switching to cycle completion. Lineage forecasts retain aggregate gains over stage and block models, while dated developmental estimates expose first-stage transfer failure. Conventional explanation receives full credit.",
      "scope_zh": "保留16/26、19/41、7/13及6/6定理/审计与反例；本轮无新定理。54段视频/18项技术重复、33/190敏感性、3,808记录/3,600联系及42/72对7/72保持范围。3,424项预测保留局部反例；新增139实验分组/485焦点行核验。物理校准、广泛比较与支持更新仍开放。",
      "scope_en": "Preserves 16/26, 19/41, 7/13 and 6/6 theorem/audit results and counterexamples; no new theorem. The 54 videos/18 technical replicates, 33/190 sensitivity, 3,808 records/3,600 links and 42/72 versus 7/72 retain their scopes. Forecasts of 3,424 outcomes retain local failures; new checks cover 139 assay cohorts/485 focal rows. Physical calibration, broad comparison and support renewal remain open.",
